   "ihh:model": "app/public/models/einstein-gothenburg-lecture-hall/einstein-gothenburg-lecture-hall.glb",
   "ihh:glbLabel": "Recreation based on a photograph: the Kongresshallen of the Gothenburg Jubilee Exhibition, 11 July 1923, Anders Wilhelm Karnell, Goteborgs stadsmuseum GhmF:148 (used as a modelling reference). The museum's record describes Einstein lecturing on relativity to the Scandinavian Congress of Naturalists in this hall that day. People are not shown; the walls the photograph does not show are plain.",
   "ihh:shownIn": [
    {
     "ihh:inductee": "einstein",
     "ihh:chapter": "honoured",
     "ihh:chapterTitle": "The Nobel Prize",
     "ihh:placeLabel": "A lecture hall in Gothenburg"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:texturesFrom": [],
   "ihh:sourcesFile": "assets-src/einstein-gothenburg-lecture-hall/SOURCES.md",
   "ihh:inventoryFile": "assets-src/einstein-gothenburg-lecture-hall/INVENTORY.md",
   "ihh:creditsSection": "app/CREDITS.md, section \"Kongresshallen, Gothenburg (app/public/models/einstein-gothenburg-lecture-hall, built from assets-src/einstein-gothenburg-lecture-hall)\"",
   "name": "A lecture hall · Gothenburg",
   "ihh:tourLabel": "A lecture hall in Gothenburg, rebuilt from a photograph of his lecture. Göteborgs stadsmuseum's records of the photographs shown here name the hall as the Kongresshallen; no verified fact names it. A newspaper report says Einstein delivered an address at Gottenberg [sic], Sweden, before a scientific body on his theory of relativity, and that King Gustaf was among those present. Every texture is drawn; people are not shown, and the walls the photograph does not show are plain."
  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-einstein:ch:honoured:opening",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "einstein:ch:honoured:opening",
   "ihh:lineKind": "opening",
   "ihh:text": "Albert Einstein received a Nobel Prize for Physics. In Gottenberg [sic], Sweden, he delivered an address before a scientific body on his theory of relativity. Walk around, if you like.",
   "ihh:source": [
    "Albert Einstein received a Nobel Prize for Physics for his services to theoretical physics, and especially for his discovery of the law of the photoelectric effect.",
    "Einstein delivered an address at Gottenberg, Sweden, before a scientific body on his theory of relativity."
   ],
