  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-muir:ch:arriving:opening",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "muir:ch:arriving:opening",
   "ihh:lineKind": "opening",
   "ihh:text": "John Muir immigrated from Scotland to Wisconsin, to the Fountain Lake farm. Its farmhouse, made of white pine, was completed in October 1849, and in early November 1849 the rest of his family arrived from Scotland. Take a moment here.",
   "ihh:source": [
    "John Muir immigrated from Scotland to Wisconsin.",
    "John Muir lived continually at the Fountain Lake farm from 1849-1856.",
    "The farmhouse on the Muir farm, made of white pine, was completed in October 1849.",
    "In early November 1849 the rest of John Muir's family arrived from Scotland."
   ],
   "citation": [
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0082"
    },
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0100"
    },
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0103"
    },
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0104"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:claimStatus": {
    "MUI-F-0082": "verified",
    "MUI-F-0100": "verified",
    "MUI-F-0103": "verified",
    "MUI-F-0104": "verified"
   },
   "ihh:usedIn": [
    {
     "ihh:inductee": "muir",
     "ihh:chapter": "arriving",
     "ihh:role": "opening"
    }
   ],
   "about": {
    "@id": "ihh:person-muir"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-muir:1:c5",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "muir:1:c5",
   "ihh:lineKind": "fact",
   "ihh:text": "His father, Daniel Muir, named the farm Fountain Lake.",
   "ihh:source": "Daniel Muir, John Muir's father, named the farm Fountain Lake.",
   "citation": [
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0102"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:claimStatus": {
    "MUI-F-0102": "verified"
   },
   "ihh:usedIn": [
    {
     "ihh:inductee": "muir",
     "ihh:chapter": "arriving",
     "ihh:role": "chapter-closing"
    }
   ],
   "about": {
    "@id": "ihh:person-muir"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-muir:5:c4",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "muir:5:c4",
   "ihh:lineKind": "fact",
   "ihh:text": "At the Fountain Lake farm, he tried, for the first time, to preserve from human development a piece of land in its wild state.",
   "ihh:source": "At the Fountain Lake farm, Muir tried, for the first time, to preserve from human development a piece of land in its wild state.",
   "citation": [
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0105"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:claimStatus": {
    "MUI-F-0105": "verified"
   },
   "ihh:usedIn": [
    {
     "ihh:inductee": "muir",
     "ihh:chapter": "arriving",
     "ihh:role": "chapter-closing"
    }
   ],
   "about": {
    "@id": "ihh:person-muir"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-muir:5:c5",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "muir:5:c5",
   "ihh:lineKind": "fact",
   "ihh:text": "John Muir identified the Fountain Lake farm as the birthplace of his interest in preserving wilderness for its own sake.",
   "ihh:source": "John Muir identified the Fountain Lake farm as the birthplace of his interest in preserving wilderness for its own sake.",
   "citation": [
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0106"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:claimStatus": {
    "MUI-F-0106": "verified"
   },
   "ihh:usedIn": [
    {
     "ihh:inductee": "muir",
     "ihh:chapter": "arriving",
     "ihh:role": "chapter-closing"
    }
   ],
   "about": {
    "@id": "ihh:person-muir"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-muir:5:c1",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "muir:5:c1",
   "ihh:lineKind": "fact",
   "ihh:text": "John Muir and his family moved to their second Wisconsin farm, Hickory Hill.",
   "ihh:source": "John Muir and his family moved to their second Wisconsin farm, Hickory Hill.",
   "citation": [
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0107"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:claimStatus": {
    "MUI-F-0107": "verified"
   },
   "ihh:usedIn": [
    {
     "ihh:inductee": "muir",
     "ihh:chapter": "arriving",
     "ihh:role": "chapter-closing"
    }
   ],
   "about": {
    "@id": "ihh:person-muir"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-muir:5:c2",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "muir:5:c2",
   "ihh:lineKind": "fact",
   "ihh:text": "He assumed more and more of the work at the new farm, Hickory Hill.",
   "ihh:source": "John Muir assumed more and more of the work at the new farm, Hickory Hill.",
   "citation": [
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0108"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:claimStatus": {
    "MUI-F-0108": "verified"
   },
   "ihh:usedIn": [
    {
     "ihh:inductee": "muir",
     "ihh:chapter": "arriving",
     "ihh:role": "chapter-closing"
    }
   ],
   "about": {
    "@id": "ihh:person-muir"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-muir:1:c2",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "muir:1:c2",
   "ihh:lineKind": "fact",
   "ihh:text": "In 1849, a ten-year-old, he left Scotland for the United States, in the company of his father, sister, and brother.",
   "ihh:source": "In 1849, in the company of his father, sister, and brother, ten-year-old John Muir left Scotland for the United States.",
   "citation": [
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0097"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:claimStatus": {
    "MUI-F-0097": "verified"
   },
   "ihh:usedIn": [
    {
     "ihh:inductee": "muir",
     "ihh:chapter": "arriving",
     "ihh:role": "map"
    }
   ],
   "about": {
    "@id": "ihh:person-muir"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-muir:1:c3",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "muir:1:c3",
   "ihh:lineKind": "fact",
   "ihh:text": "The Muirs landed in New York City in 1849, and went by boat to Albany, and then across the Erie Canal to Buffalo.",
   "ihh:source": "In 1849 the Muirs landed in New York City and went by boat to Albany and then across the Erie Canal to Buffalo.",
   "citation": [
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0098"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:claimStatus": {
    "MUI-F-0098": "verified"
   },
   "ihh:usedIn": [
    {
     "ihh:inductee": "muir",
     "ihh:chapter": "arriving",
     "ihh:role": "map"
    }
   ],
   "about": {
    "@id": "ihh:person-muir"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-muir:1:c4",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "muir:1:c4",
   "ihh:lineKind": "fact",
   "ihh:text": "From Buffalo, Daniel Muir and his three children traveled across the Great Lakes to Milwaukee, and then overland to Kingston.",
   "ihh:source": "From Buffalo, Daniel Muir and his three children traveled across the Great Lakes to Milwaukee and then overland to Kingston.",
   "citation": [
    {
     "@id": "ihh:MUI-F-0099"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:claimStatus": {
    "MUI-F-0099": "verified"
   },
