   "name": "Glacier Point, Yosemite (July 1903)",
   "description": "Photo room — based on a Library of Congress stereograph (public domain): Underwood & Underwood, “President Roosevelt’s choicest recreation - amid nature’s rugged grandeur on Glacier Point, Yosemite”, c1903 July 18 (right image). It shows President Roosevelt on the ledge; John Muir is not in this photograph. The depth is estimated from the photograph; past its edges there is nothing to show.",
