  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-muir:ch:legacy:opening",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "muir:ch:legacy:opening",
   "ihh:lineKind": "opening",
   "ihh:text": "In 1911, John Muir published My First Summer in the Sierra. He was a preservationist, and President of the California Branch of the Society for the Preservation of National Parks; here is the Hetch Hetchy Valley. Have a look around.",
   "ihh:source": [
    "In 1911 Muir published My First Summer in the Sierra.",
    "The petition signed by John Muir urged Congress to defeat the Raker Bill, which called for a dam to be built across the Hetch Hetchy Valley.",
    "John Muir was a preservationist.",
    "Mr. John Muir of Martinez was President of the California Branch of the Society for the Preservation of National Parks."
   ],
   "citation": [
