   "name": "The Security Council chamber, as photographed 1977-81",
   "ihh:tourLabel": "Recreation based on a photograph: U.N. Security Council Chamber, Bernard Gotfryd, between 1977 and 1981 (Library of Congress, LC-GB05-5929). From 1993 to 1997, Albright served as the U.S. Permanent Representative to the United Nations; the chamber is shown as photographed before those years."
  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-albright:ch:big-work:opening",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "albright:ch:big-work:opening",
   "ihh:lineKind": "opening",
   "ihh:text": "In 1993, Madeleine Albright, who became a U.S. citizen in 1957, was appointed Ambassador to the United Nations by President Clinton. Walk around, if you like.",
   "ihh:source": [
    "Albright became a U.S. citizen in 1957.",
    "In 1993 Albright was appointed Ambassador to the United Nations by President Clinton.",
    "Madeleine Albright testified in front of the Senate Foreign Relations Committee during her confirmation hearing to be U.S. ambassador to the United Nations."
   ],
