     "ihh:sourcesRow": {
      "Frames": "16, 17, 18",
      "What they show of the room": "The window bay from behind the sofas: three tall sash windows (three panes across, three up per sash), drapes on both sides of each window, the U.S. flag and a dark flag at the piers, palms in pale jardinieres, the desk, its high-backed chair, two cane-back armchairs, the rug's border; at the right the east wall with a console, an equestrian bronze and a landscape.",
      "Used for": "Comparison camera (16); bay, flags, palms, desk group; east console. Textures: view through the window, drape fabric, the east landscape (impression), the bronze (cut-out card)."
     },
     "ihh:holder": "National Archives, William J. Clinton Library, White House Photograph Office (Clinton Administration), roll WHPO-P02724, photographer Bob McNeely, 20 April 1993; file unit NAID 187792855, https://catalog.archives.gov/id/187792855 (title \"WHPO-P02724\"; scope note: \"President Clinton speaking with Ambassador to the United Nations Madeleine Albright, Secretary of State Warren Christopher, National Security Advisor Tony Lake, George Stephanopoulos and others in the Oval Office.\")",
     "ihh:holderFrom": "SOURCES.md section",
     "ihh:rights": "Use restriction (holder's words): \"Unrestricted\". The project reads NARA \"Unrestricted\" federal photographs as public domain (DECISIONS 2026-10-09), so the frames may supply textures and the comparison sheets in `previews/` may be committed with this credit.",
     "ihh:rightsFrom": "SOURCES.md section",
     "ihh:texture": "the other frames of roll WHPO-P02724 (09-15, 17-23, 25-27, 29-31): texture crops listed in SOURCES.md under the same holder statement",
