  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-albright:ch:history:opening",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "albright:ch:history:opening",
   "ihh:lineKind": "opening",
   "ihh:text": "On July 8, 1997, Madeleine Albright talked to reporters in Madrid. At the NATO summit, the decision was to invite Poland, Hungary, and the Czech Republic. On July 14, 1997, she addressed the People of Prague at Obecni Dum. She was U.S. Secretary of State from 1997 to 2001. Have a look around.",
   "ihh:source": [
    "On July 14, 1997, Secretary of State Madeleine K. Albright addressed the People of Prague at Obecni Dum.",
    "Madeleine Albright was U.S. Secretary of State from 1997 to 2001.",
    "On July 8, 1997, at the Miguel Angel Hotel, Madrid, Spain, Secretary of State Madeleine Albright and Secretary of Defense William Cohen talked to reporters about the decision, made at the NATO summit, to invite Poland, Hungary, and the Czech Republic to begin accession negotiations to join the NATO alliance."
   ],
   "citation": [
    {
     "@id": "ihh:ALB-F-0095"
    },
    {
     "@id": "ihh:ALB-F-0162"
    },
    {
     "@id": "ihh:ALB-F-0200"
    }
   ],
