   "ihh:model": "app/public/models/albright-east-room-2012/albright-east-room-2012.glb",
   "ihh:glbLabel": "Recreation based on photographs: the East Room of the White House as set up for the Presidential Medal of Freedom ceremony of 29 May 2012 (White House photographs, National Archives). The room's architecture is modelled from photographs of 1904 and 1908 (Library of Congress) and checked against the 2012 photographs, which show the same pilasters and cornice; the drapes, mirror, candelabra, flags and lectern follow the 2012 photographs. People and the audience's seating are not modelled.",
   "ihh:shownIn": [
    {
     "ihh:inductee": "albright",
     "ihh:chapter": "honoured",
     "ihh:chapterTitle": "The Presidential Medal of Freedom",
     "ihh:placeLabel": "The East Room, White House (May 29, 2012)"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:texturesFrom": [
    {
     "@id": "ihh:ALB-M-0082",
     "ihh:mediaId": "ALB-M-0082",
     "ihh:what": "drape fabric, the mirror's reflection (softened), the seal (blurred to an impression)"
    }
   ],
   "ihh:sourcesFile": "assets-src/albright-east-room-2012/SOURCES.md",
   "ihh:inventoryFile": "assets-src/albright-east-room-2012/INVENTORY.md",
   "ihh:creditsSection": "app/CREDITS.md, section \"East Room, 29 May 2012 (app/public/models/albright-east-room-2012, built from assets-src/albright-east-room-2012)\"",
   "name": "The East Room, White House · May 29, 2012",
   "ihh:tourLabel": "Recreation based on photographs: the East Room of the White House as set up for the Presidential Medal of Freedom ceremony of May 29, 2012 (White House photographs, National Archives, public domain). Madeleine Albright was a recipient of the Presidential Medal of Freedom that President Barack Obama presented during a ceremony in the East Room of the White House, May 29, 2012. The 2012 photographs show other honorees receiving their medals; she is not in them. The room’s architecture is modelled from photographs of 1904 and 1908 (Library of Congress) and checked against the 2012 photographs, so details may differ. People and the audience’s seating are not modelled."
  },
  {
   "@id": "ihh:line-albright:ch:honoured:opening",
   "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
   "ihh:key": "albright:ch:honoured:opening",
   "ihh:lineKind": "opening",
   "ihh:text": "Madeleine Albright was a recipient of the Presidential Medal of Freedom. On May 29, 2012, eleven years after her farewell remarks as Secretary of State, President Barack Obama presented it during a ceremony in the East Room of the White House. Take a moment and look around.",
   "ihh:source": [
    "Secretary of State Madeleine K. Albright's farewell remarks at the U.S. Department of State were on January 19, 2001.",
    "Madeleine Albright was a recipient of the Presidential Medal of Freedom that President Barack Obama presented during a ceremony in the East Room of the White House, May 29, 2012."
   ],
   "citation": [
