   "ihh:glbLabel": "Recreation based on a photograph: an air-raid shelter in a London subway tunnel, with bunk beds, Toni Frissell, between 1940 and 1945 (Library of Congress). One source says Madeleine Albright hid in shelters as German bombs fell on London; no source names the shelter, and this is not one she is known to have used. The people in the bunks are not shown. Colours are interpretive: the photograph is black and white.",
