   "ihh:model": "app/public/models/muir-glacier-point-1903/muir-glacier-point-1903.glb",
   "ihh:glbLabel": "Recreation based on photographs: Glacier Point, Yosemite, 1903 -- Underwood & Underwood stereographs of President Roosevelt on the ledge (July 1903) and the photograph of Theodore Roosevelt and John Muir standing on it (1903), Library of Congress. In 1903 Muir and Roosevelt were in Yosemite. The far view is the July 1903 photograph itself, with Roosevelt's figure painted out; beyond its frame the sky and haze carry only the photograph's own tones, and the rock beyond the photographed ledge is plain. The people are not modelled. Colours are interpretive: the prints are sepia.",
